      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Neither class is universally prescribed over the other as a standalone first-line therapy for type 2 diabetes. While traditional guidelines long mandated metformin as the primary first-line agent, modern American Diabetes Association (ADA) and European Association for the Study of Diabetes (EASD) guidelines recommend choosing SGLT2 inhibitors (SGLT2i) or GLP-1 receptor agonists (GLP-1RA) as first-line or early options based on specific patient comorbidities (such as atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease, heart failure, or chronic kidney disease) rather than a rigid glucose-lowering hierarchy.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "Neither class is universally prescribed over the other as a standalone first-line therapy for type 2 diabetes"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
