        "snippet": "How to Choose Between Them"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Choose an SGLT2 Inhibitor first if: The patient has predominant heart failure (with reduced ejection fraction) or chronic kidney disease (CKD), or prefers a daily oral pill.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Choose a GLP-1 Receptor Agonist first if: The patient has established atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (ASCVD), high stroke risk, significant obesity requiring substantial weight loss, or needs stronger HbA1c lowering.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Combination Therapy: Guidelines note that using both classes together provides synergistic cardiorenal, glycemic, and weight-loss benefits when cost and tolerability allow.",
